 ## What they've asked for
+Second distinct site: "My Commute" (`hiiii-demo`) — a super-light single-person
+hydrofoil crossing San Francisco Bay from Lake Merritt (Oakland) to Oracle's
+Redwood Shores campus. Read together with `create-space` below, a pattern:
+both are 3D vehicle/environment simulations grounded in a real or
+personally-resonant place (a real Bay Area commute; an O'Neill cylinder as a
+lived-in world), controlled by a single slider (throttle / spin speed) plus
+drag-to-look and pinch/scroll-zoom, rather than active multi-key piloting or
+driving controls. Reinforces the ambient-over-manual preference noted below —
+across two different mechanics now (proximity-reveal vs. an autopilot route),
+the throughline is: light, low-effort input: (one slider) driving something
+that unfolds mostly on its own, watched via free-look camera rather than
+steered by hand.
